        "**Low-pass filtering** weakens higher frequencies more than lower ones. Bates and colleagues applied mild low-pass filtering to the probe echo. This reduced FM2 relative to FM1 by an average of about 1.5 dB, approximating the harmonic imbalance of nearby lateral clutter. The filter imitated a nearby object off to the side. The filter reduces FM2 most.",
